358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Existing sentiment and mental-health analysis systems often rely primarily on textual information from social media. Such approaches may lose relevant emotional and contextual information contained in images, memes, and other visual content. The project therefore aims to develop an AI-driven multimodal framework that jointly analyses textual and visual information for sentiment-based mental health monitoring. The proposed system will also compare multimodal analysis with individual text-based and image-based approaches.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning techniques are increasingly being used to analyse social media content and identify meaningful patterns. Natural Language Processing enables systems to analyse textual information and determine sentiments, emotions, and linguistic characteristics. However, social media communication also includes images, memes, and other visual information that may contain important emotional context. Multimodal AI addresses this limitation by combining information from multiple modalities such as text and images.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
