377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Images shared on social media can contain emotional and contextual information that may not be explicitly expressed through words. Computer Vision and Deep Learning models such as Convolutional Neural Networks can be used to extract meaningful visual features from such content. Visual analysis can therefore provide additional information for understanding the emotional context of social media posts. However, image-only approaches may fail to understand the textual meaning associated with the visual content.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Text-based mental-health analysis uses Natural Language Processing and Machine Learning techniques to identify emotional and linguistic patterns in social media posts. Traditional approaches use techniques such as word representations and statistical features, while modern approaches use deep learning and transformer-based models such as BERT. These methods can identify useful textual indicators associated with different sentiments and mental-health-related states. However, they cannot directly utilise information contained in visual content.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
