426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (The project follows an experimental and comparative research approach for developing and evaluating a multimodal AI framework. The study will involve dataset preparation, preprocessing, feature extraction, model development, multimodal fusion, and performance evaluation. Separate unimodal models will also be considered to provide a meaningful comparison with the proposed multimodal approach.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (A comparative experimental approach is suitable because the primary aim is to determine whether combining different modalities provides an improvement over individual modalities. The approach allows textual, visual, and multimodal models to be evaluated using common performance metrics. The resulting comparison will provide quantitative evidence regarding the effectiveness of multimodal analysis.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 157 0 R
/E (The proposed framework will accept social media content containing textual and visual information as input. The text will undergo Natural Language Processing, while the associated images will be processed using suitable Computer Vision techniques. Features extracted from both modalities will be combined through a feature-fusion mechanism and passed to a classification stage. The final system will generate a mental-health-related sentiment or classification output based on the selected dataset categories.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
